README.OSK -- rex, rexd, rexdc, chp and remdate for OS-9/NetPeter Reinig's remote-execution utilities for OS-9/Net, 1990, fromMicroware's archive (SRC/rex.tar.Z).  Source only in the archive; the fivemodules in CMDS/NETWORK were built here by recipe (tools/rebuild), -qm, sothey need no cio.Changes to the source: none.  Changes to the build:  - The makefile defines HAS_UTMP, for a SunOS-compatible utmp.h this    toolchain has not got; the build leaves it out, so rexdc keeps no    wtmp record of remote logins.  - The makefile sets REX and REXDC to full paths under /dd/usr and    /dd/etc; the build leaves REX alone, so chp runs `rex' by name.  - rexd and rexdc are built as prexd and prexdc, with    -DREXDC="prexdc" so the daemon starts its own server.  Microware's    OS-9/Net SDK has commands named rexd and rexdc, and a reader who loads    theirs from /h1 would otherwise get one of each.  The usage text still    says `rexd', as the source does.  - Links Microware's net.l (the OS-9/Net calls) and os9lib.l    (getpwuid, getpwnam, endpwent).Not tested: everything here needs an OS-9/Net network (/n0).